          %h2#Idea Idea
          %p
            By the discussion at
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categorical+hom-spaces"} (∞,1)-categorical hom-spaces
                in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-toposes"} (∞,1)-toposes
                (for “
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+cohomology"}> nonabelian cohomology
                ”)
            %li
              %p
                or their
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stabilizations"} stabilizations
                to
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} stable (∞,1)-categories
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum+objects"} spectrum objects
                (for “
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+%28Eilenberg-Steenrod%29+cohomology"}> generalized (Eilenberg-Steenrod) cohomology
                ”)
            %li
              %p
                or generally in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} symmetric monoidal (∞,1)-categories
          %p
            and maybe fully generally in any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            whatsoever.
          %p
            So for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in \mathcal{C}
            any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
            of any other object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+space"} mapping space
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}(X,A)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sections"} sections
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_{/X}(X, X \times A)
            of the trivial
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} fiber ∞-bundle
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %em twisted cohomology
            then is to consider general
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+%E2%88%9E-bundles"} fiber ∞-bundles
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi χ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and take the
            = succeed "-twisted" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi χ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to the type of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sections"} sections
            of this.
          %table
            %thead
              %tr
                %th
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
                %th twisted cohomology
            %tbody
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+types"} homotopy types
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+spaces"} mapping spaces
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+types"} homotopy types
                  of spaces of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sections"} sections
          %p
            Given an
            = succeed "-topos" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}^I
            is an
            = succeed "-topos," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn ∞
                  %msup
                    %mi Grpd
                    %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty Grpd^I
            and it also sits over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            by the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codomain+fibration"} codomain fibration
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extension"} extension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            by itself:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi H
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mi incl
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi H
                            %mi I
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mi cod
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi H
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\mathbf{H}
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{incl}}
                  \\\
                  \\mathbf{H}^I
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{cod}}
                  \\\
                  \\mathbf{H}
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            The intrinsic cohomology of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}^I
            under this fibration is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+cohomology"} nonabelian
            twisted cohomology as discussed in some detail in
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Principal+%E2%88%9E-bundles+--+theory%2C+presentations+and+applications"} Principal ∞-bundles – theory, presentations and applications
          %p
            Notice that “stable cohomology”, which is traditionally called
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+%28Eilenberg-Steenrod%29+cohomology"} generalized (Eilenberg-Steenrod) cohomology
            may be thought of as the lowest order
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Goodwillie+calculus"} Goodwillie
            approximation to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+cohomology"} nonabelian cohomology
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+%28Eilenberg-Steenrod%29+cohomology"} generalized (Eilenberg-Steenrod) cohomology
            is a map into a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+type"} stable homotopy type
          %p
            In this sense the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+%28infinity%2C1%29-topos"} tangent (infinity,1)-topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \mathbf{H}
            is the lowest order linear approximation to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codomain+fibration"} codomain fibration
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Stab
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi H
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mi incl
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi T
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi H
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mi cod
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi H
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\Stab(\mathbf{H})
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{incl}}
                  \\\
                  T\mathbf{H}
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{cod}}
                  \\\
                  \\mathbf{H}
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            Higher-order approximations should involve a notion of higher-order forms of the tangent (∞,1)-topos, in parallel with the relationship between the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/jet+bundles"} jet bundles
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+bundle"} tangent bundle
            of a manifold. It is clear that whatever we may say in detail about the
            = succeed "th-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/jet+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} jet (∞,1)-topos
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi J
                      %mi k
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J^k \mathbf{H}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+cohomology"} nonabelian cohomology
            and stable i.e.
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+%28Eilenberg-Steenrod%29+cohomology"} generalized (Eilenberg-Steenrod) cohomology
          %p
            It seems that a layered analysis of nonabelian cohomology this way in higher homotopy theory should eventually be rather important, even if it hasn’t received any attention at all yet. It seems plausible that a generalization of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Weil+theory"} Chern-Weil theory
            which approximates classes of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+infinity-bundles"} principal infinity-bundles
            not just by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+characteristic+classes"} universal characteristic classes
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+cohomology"} ordinary cohomology
            and hence in stable cohomology, but that one wants to consider the whole Goodwillie Taylor tower of approximations to it.
          %h2#Definition Definition
          %p
            We discuss concrete realizations of the above
            %a{:href => "#Idea"} general idea
            in some cases of interest:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %em
