          %h3#chronology_of_literature_on_twisted_cohomology Chronology of literature on twisted cohomology
          %p
            The oldest meaning of twisted cohomology is that of
            %strong cohomology with local coefficients
            (see above).
          %p For more on the history of that notion see
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/History+of+cohomology+with+local+coefficients"} History of cohomology with local coefficients
          %p In the following we shall abbreviate
          %ul
            %li tc = twisted cohomology
          %p
            Searching MathSciNet for
            %em twisted cohomology
            led to the following chronology: It missed older references in which the phrase was not used but the concept was in the sense of local coefficient systems – ancient and honorable.
          %p Most notably missing are
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kurt+Reidemeister"} Kurt Reidemeister
              (1938) Topologie der Polyeder und kombinatorische
